@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Management browser login with OpenID Connect
+
+Management OIDC is optional and does not change model API authentication. Existing
+management keys remain available for automation. Register an authorization-code
+client with your identity provider and configure these process environment variables:
+
+| Variable | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `MANAGEMENT_OIDC_ISSUER` | HTTPS issuer URL; unset disables OIDC |
+| `MANAGEMENT_OIDC_CLIENT_ID` | Registered client ID |
+| `MANAGEMENT_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret for a confidential client |
+| `MANAGEMENT_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL` | `https://<admin-host>/v0/management/callback` |
+| `MANAGEMENT_OIDC_ALLOWED_SUBJECTS` | Comma-separated allowed `sub` values |
+
+Subjects are the exact immutable identifiers issued by the configured provider,
+not email addresses or display names. Configuring OIDC enables management routes
+independently of the management-key remote-access setting. Configuration changes
+require a restart. Issuer and redirect URLs must use HTTPS; terminate TLS at the
+server or a reverse proxy. Serve the management UI on the redirect URL's origin.
+
+A session-aware management UI discovers `GET /v0/management/session`, which returns
+`oidcEnabled` and `authenticated` booleans without requiring credentials. Navigate
+to `GET /v0/management/login` to start login. The callback returns to
+`/management.html`. Cookie-authenticated API requests must send
+`X-Management-CSRF: 1`, including GET requests; foreign Origin headers and cross-site
+fetches are rejected. `POST /v0/management/logout` requires the same header and
+revokes the local browser session. It does not sign out of the identity provider.
+
+Sessions and five-minute login transactions are held in memory, each capped at
+1024 entries. Use one instance or sticky routing. Sessions expire at the earlier
+of one hour and ID-token expiry, and restarting the process revokes all sessions.
+Provider access and refresh tokens are not retained. The backend verifies PKCE,
+browser-bound state, nonce, token signature, issuer, audience, and expiry before
+checking the subject allowlist. Forwarded identity headers do not authenticate.
